{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L1-0001", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L1", "question": "If half of a number is 18, what is the number?", "choices": {"A": "9", "B": "36", "C": "20", "D": "72"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "If half is 18, the number is 18 × 2 = 36.", "tags": ["basic", "operation"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L1-0002", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L1", "question": "What is 25% of 100?", "choices": {"A": "25", "B": "75", "C": "4", "D": "125"}, "answer": "A", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "100 × 0.25 = 25.", "tags": ["percentage", "basic"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L1-0003", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L1", "question": "In the pattern 5, 10, 15, 20, ..., what is the 6th term?", "choices": {"A": "25", "B": "30", "C": "35", "D": "24"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "The pattern is multiples of 5; the 6th term is 5 × 6 = 30.", "tags": ["pattern", "sequence"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L2-0004", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L2", "question": "In a class of 40 students, 60% are boys. How many girls are there?", "choices": {"A": "24", "B": "16", "C": "20", "D": "40"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "Girls make up 40%: 40 × 0.40 = 16.", "tags": ["percentage", "inference"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L2-0005", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L2", "question": "In the pattern 2, 6, 18, 54, ..., what is the next term?", "choices": {"A": "108", "B": "162", "C": "150", "D": "216"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "Each term is 3 times the previous: 54 × 3 = 162.", "tags": ["pattern", "geometric"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L2-0006", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L2", "question": "A worker makes 20 parts in 4 hours. At the same rate, how many parts in 7 hours?", "choices": {"A": "28", "B": "35", "C": "40", "D": "70"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "Rate is 20 / 4 = 5 parts per hour; in 7 hours, 5 × 7 = 35 parts.", "tags": ["rate", "proportion"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L3-0007", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L3", "question": "A price first rises by 20% and then falls by 20% off the new price. What is the net change from the start?", "choices": {"A": "+4%", "B": "-4%", "C": "No change", "D": "-20%"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "1.20 × 0.80 = 0.96, so the price drops to 96% of the original — a 4% net decrease.", "tags": ["percentage", "multi-step", "distractor-net-rate"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "public"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L3-0008", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L3", "question": "In the pattern 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, ..., what is the 8th term?", "choices": {"A": "49", "B": "64", "C": "81", "D": "36"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "The pattern is perfect squares (n²); the 8th term is 8² = 64.", "tags": ["pattern", "squares"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L4-0009", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L4", "question": "A city has 250,000 people, and 1 in every 5 owns a car. Approximately how many cars are there?", "choices": {"A": "25,000", "B": "50,000", "C": "125,000", "D": "1,250,000"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "If 1 in 5 owns a car, the number of cars is one-fifth of the population: 250,000 / 5 = 50,000.", "tags": ["estimation", "ratio", "multi-step"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
{"id": "MIHENK-NUM-EN-L4-0010", "language": "en", "discipline": "Sayısal Akıl Yürütme", "format": "multiple_choice", "difficulty": "L4", "question": "A student's average over 3 exams is 70. If they score 90 on the 4th exam, what is the new average over all four?", "choices": {"A": "72", "B": "75", "C": "80", "D": "70"}, "answer": "B", "answer_short": null, "explanation": "First three total 3 × 70 = 210; new total is 210 + 90 = 300; average = 300 / 4 = 75.", "tags": ["average", "multi-step"], "source": "orijinal-AI-üretim", "version_added": "1.0", "split": "private"}
